<title>Video.play Function</title>


<subheader>Format</subheader>

<logicsyntax>
b = video_name.play(『<arg>message</arg>』);
</logicsyntax>


<subheader>Description</subheader>

The <logiccolor>Video.play</logiccolor> function launches a player to play the video in a <link Video.csdoc>Video</link> object. Before calling this function, the object must contain video data recorded using <logiccolor>Video.recordInteractive</logiccolor> or loaded using <logiccolor>Video.load</logiccolor>. If the optional argument <arg>message</arg> is provided as a string expression, the message text is displayed above the video player.

CSPro can load and play most video files, but only <link "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WebM">WebM</link> files are fully supported by CSPro (in functions such as <logiccolor>Video.length</logiccolor>).


<subheader>Return Value</subheader>

The function returns a logical value of <logiccolor>1</logiccolor> (<logiccolor>true</logiccolor>) if the video player is successfully launched, or  <logiccolor>0</logiccolor> (<logiccolor>false</logiccolor>) if there is an error opening the player or if the Video object does not contain a video recording.


